redient names and prices (100g). The mood is lighthearted and comedic, emphasizing the physical effort required for the cooking preparation.', 'similarity score': 0.6907883882522583}, {'clip_467_469': 'clip_467_469', 'text': 'In this sequence, actress **Nam Bora** is shown making a large quantity of Korean dumplings (*mandu*) in her home. She sits on a white mat on the wooden floor, leaning over a low white table covered with multiple trays of finished dumplings and a large metal mixing bowl. Dressed in comfortable home clothes with her hair tied back, she works quickly and continuously, her hands busy wrapping or arranging the dumplings.\n\nThe setting is a clean, modern Korean living space with houseplants on a low shelf, a standing air conditioner, white curtains, and minimal furniture. An inset in the corner shows a male commentator in a red jacket reacting to the scene.\n\n**Visible text** includes commentary about the physical difficulty of the task ("저 자세로 계속 있는 거 정말 힘들어" - "It\'s really hard to stay in that position continuously") and praise for her skill ("만장인 남보라" - a pun combining *mandu* and *jangin* [master/expert] with her name). The show title "편스토랑" (*Pyeon Storang*) appears in the top left corner.\n\n**Mood**: Industrious and domestic, with an undertone of impressed commentary regarding the sheer volume of food preparation and the endurance required to sit in that position for extended periods.', 'similarity score': 0.6831745505332947}, {'clip_133_137': 'clip_133_137', 'text': 'In this kitchen cooking segment, a woman demonstrates how to remove excess moisture from tofu. \n\n**Actions:** The sequence begins with a close-up of hands holding tofu wrapped in a white cloth (133s). The woman then stands at a kitchen sink, vigorously squeezing and twisting the cloth bundle with both hands to extract liquid (134s-136s). By 137s, she continues squeezing with focused effort while a small inset shows a male commentator laughing heartily at the scene.\n\n**People/Objects:** The main subject is a woman with dark hair tied back, wearing a white short-sleeved shirt and a sage green apron, plus a smartwatch. She handles a white cloth pouch containing tofu over a stainless steel sink. A large metal bowl filled with chopped green vegetables sits on the counter beside her.\n\n**Setting:** A modern domestic kitchen featuring white countertops, dark cabinetry, a stainless steel refrigerator, and various cooking ingredients and tools arranged on the counter.\n\n**Visible Text:** Korean text appears throughout: in the top-left corner reads "편스토랑" (show title), while the top banner displays "13번째 참가자" (13th participant) and "황금 레시피 만능 100배." The first frame includes instructional text: "수분이 많은 두부는 면포에 싸서 물기를 제거" (Tofu with lots of moisture—wrap in cloth to remove water).\n\n**Mood:** Practical and instructional, shifting to lighthearted in the final frame due to the laughing reaction shot.', 'similarity score': 0.6818919777870178}, {'clip_432_435': 'clip_432_435', 'text': 'In this sequence, a woman wearing a white collared shirt and a pale green apron is seated on the floor at a low white table, engaged in food preparation (likely shaping dumplings or similar items). \n\n**Frame 432s** shows a wider shot of the scene: she sits on a cushion in a bright, minimalist room with wooden floors and potted plants, working at a table holding a metal mixing bowl and small plates. Pink Korean text appears on screen: *"알겠습니다 배달 가겠습니다"* ("I understand, I\'ll go deliver it"). The top left corner displays the show title *"편스토랑"* (Pyeon Restaurant) along with text about making "보리밥라면" (barley rice ramen) for 500 won.\n\n**Frames 433s–435s** shift to a close-up of her upper body as she carefully handles a small piece of dough or filling in her hands. She looks down intently at her work, her expression focused and gentle. The background features houseplants, including one with dark purple leaves in a terracotta pot and white flowers in a vase, creatin